!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
Keys are pointers
description: every key is a path portion — [n] selects a position, ': x' a name
- |
  Every key is a pointer: the same text that names an entry (`key: value`) is a path
  portion a pointer can travel (`*key`). The `*` sigil dereferences — beyond YAML's bare
  alias word it takes a full **pointer expression**, resolved purely structurally: a bare
  `*a` is the sibling key `a`, and scopes reach wider
  (the [pointers part](::language:pointers)).
- !!yo
  feline: *pets[1]                   # a sibling's second element
  manager: *: pets[1]                # : = current document root
  remote: *::: pet.store.com: pets   # ::: = the world — never fetched
- |
  Positions are integer keys and names are string keys, with one access form each: `[n]`
  selects the integer key n, `: x` the string key x. The old worry of an integer key `1:`
  versus a string key `'1':` dissolves — it is simply `[1]` versus `: 1`.
